In `file_ascmagic_with_encoding`, the `encode_utf8` function is called:
```c
mlen = ulen * 6;
if ((utf8_buf = CAST(unsigned char *, malloc(mlen))) == NULL) {
        file_oomem(ms, mlen);
        goto done;
}
if ((utf8_end = encode_utf8(utf8_buf, mlen, ubuf, ulen)) == NULL)
        goto done;
```

`encode_utf8` writes up to 6 bytes per character. `mlen = ulen * 6` is exactly enough. So no overflow there.

Then:
```c
