This calls `file_softmagic` with the UTF-8 encoded buffer. This is where the magic rules are matched against the UTF-8 encoded text.

Let me look at the `file_softmagic` -> `match` -> `mget` -> `mcopy` path for the UTF-8 buffer. The `mcopy` function copies data from the UTF-8 buffer into `p->s`. If the magic rule has a string type, it copies up to `sizeof(*p)` bytes.

