}
if (nbytes - offset < sizeof(*p))
        nbytes = nbytes - offset;
else
        nbytes = sizeof(*p);

(void)memcpy(p, s + offset, nbytes);
```

This is safe - it checks `offset >= nbytes` and clamps `nbytes` to `sizeof(*p)`.

